    "result_text": "All 62 tests pass and the build succeeds. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent create for `POST /api/owners`: when a request repeats with an already-seen `Idempotency-Key` header, the originally created owner is returned with **200** instead of a duplicate being created (which the duplicate-identity rule would otherwise reject with 409).\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (no `@RestController`/`@Transactional`), I added:\n\n**New function steps** (`rest/function/owner/`):\n- `IdempotencyStore` \u2014 a `@Component` process-local map of key \u2192 owner id.\n- `CheckIdempotencyKey` \u2014 new first step (before validation/persistence). Reads the optional `@RequestHeader(\"Idempotency-Key\")`; on a seen key it throws `IdempotentReplayException` to short-circuit the pipeline, otherwise publishes the key via `Out<String>`. Ungoverned since it does no DB work.\n- `RecordIdempotencyKey` \u2014 runs after `SaveOwner` (once the id exists), recording key \u2192 owner id.\n\n**Escalation** (`rest/escalation/`):\n- `IdempotentReplayException` (checked) carrying the owner id.\n- `IdempotentReplayExceptionHandler` \u2014 loads that owner and responds `200 OK` with the `OwnerDto`.\n- YAML handler at `officefloor/escalation/\u2026IdempotentReplayException.yml`.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 inserted `checkIdempotency` as the entry step (`next: validate`) and `recordIdempotency` between `save` and `audit` in `owners.POST.yml`.\n\nRequests without the header behave exactly as before (verified: all 50 existing checkpoint suites still green).\n\nKey design checks I confirmed against the runtime: `@RequestHeader` is honored by the OfficeFloor Spring MVC bridge (`SpringMvcArguments`), and the check step is deliberately left ungoverned so its short-circuit throw never marks the pipeline's write transaction rollback-only, letting the replay handler read the just-created owner within the same test transaction.",
