    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, read from `owners.POST.yml` and each step's function class.\n\n## Endpoint-wide guards\n- **Authorization** (`composition.authorize`): the whole endpoint requires `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`. An unauthorized caller never reaches step 1.\n- **Transaction governance**: every step *except* the first (`checkIdempotency`) runs under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so all validation reads and all writes commit as a single transaction at the end of the pipeline.\n\n## Ordered pipeline\n\n**1. CheckIdempotency** (`CheckIdempotencyKey`) \u2014 *no transaction*\n- Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header. If present and already recorded in the `IdempotencyStore`, throws `IdempotentReplayException` \u2192 short-circuits and returns the original owner (200) instead of creating a duplicate.\n- Otherwise publishes the key (or `\"\"` for none) for later recording.\n\n**2. Validate** (`ValidateOwnerFields`) \u2014 binds `@RequestBody` (the one and only body read)\n- Normalizes the **address** first (trim/collapse/upper-case/expand abbreviations; prefers structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`, composing them into flat `address`, else normalizes flat `address` and clears the structured lines).\n- Rejects **blank** (absent or whitespace-only) `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`.\n- Normalizes **telephone** to E.164 (strips separators, assumes `+61` for national numbers, enforces 8\u201315 digits and fixed national lengths for `+61`=9 / `+1`=10); invalid \u2192 `telephone` error.\n- Runs the DTO's schema constraints (pattern, max length, `@Email`) via the `Validator`, adding any violated fields.\n- Validates **postcode** (only when present): schema enforces 4-digit format; then must be in range for the city's region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown city accepts any).\n- Any accumulated errors \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400). On success, **normalizes email to lower-case** and publishes the validated body.\n\n**3. RejectDisposableEmailDomain** \u2014 if email domain \u2208 {mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com} \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` (400). Absent/domain-less email passes.\n\n**4. RejectFutureRegistrationDate** \u2014 if supplied `registrationDate` is after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400). Absent date passes.\n\n**5. ResolveRegistrationDate** \u2014 computes effective date (supplied, else today), **rolls forward** weekends/public holidays to the next business day, and publishes it as a `LocalDate` used by later steps.\n\n**6. RejectDuplicateIdentity** \u2014 scans all non-soft-deleted owners:\n- **Identity duplicate** (same `normalizedTelephone|email|householdId`) \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409), *always*, even with `sharesHousehold`.\n- **Household duplicate** (same `householdId` = same last name + postcode) \u2192 409, *unless* `sharesHousehold: true`.\n\n**7. RejectCityAtCapacity** \u2014 if the city (case-insensitive) already has \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n\n**8. RejectDailyLimit** (`RejectDailyOwnerLimit`) \u2014 if \u2265 100 owners already exist for the resolved business day \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429).\n\n**9. Build** (`BuildOwner`) \u2014 maps DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity and stamps the resolved (business-day-adjusted) `registrationDate`, overriding any supplied value.\n\n**10. AssignCustomerCode** \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city; HASH8 = first 8 hex of SHA-256(telephone+lastName)); appends `-<n>` to deduplicate against existing codes.\n\n**11. AssignMembershipNumber** \u2014 sets `membershipNumber` = `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, YY = last two digits of the fiscal year (starts 1 July) of the registration date.\n\n**12. AssignHousehold** \u2014 sets `householdId` deterministically from last name + postcode (unconditional, even for a lone owner).\n\n**13. AssignHouseholdSize** \u2014 sets `householdMemberCount` = existing owners sharing the `householdId` **plus this one** (lone owner = 1).\n\n**14. CountNamesakes** (`AssignNamesakeCount`) \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive), excluding this not-yet-persisted owner.\n\n**15. FlagBulkSignup** (`AssignBulkSignupWarning`) \u2014 sets `bulkSignupWarning` = true if > 80 owners already share this business day.\n\n**16. FlagPossibleDuplicate** (`AssignPossibleDuplicate`) \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold: true`, sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` when a non-deleted owner shares last name + postcode but has a *different* telephone (lowest matching id wins); otherwise `false`/null.\n\n**17. Save** (`SaveOwner`) \u2014 `ownerRepository.save(owner)` (generates the id).\n\n**18. RecordIdempotency** (`RecordIdempotencyKey`) \u2014 if a key was supplied, records `key \u2192 owner.id` in the `IdempotencyStore` for future replay detection.\n\n**19. Audit** (`AuditOwnerCreated`) \u2014 emits an `AUDIT` log line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber.\n\n**20. Respond** (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) \u2014 maps to `OwnerDto` and returns **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n### Summary of the two categories\n- **Validations / rejections (in order):** idempotent-replay short-circuit \u2192 required-field/format/telephone/postcode validation (400) \u2192 disposable email (400) \u2192 future registration date (400) \u2192 duplicate identity/household (409) \u2192 city capacity (409) \u2192 daily limit (429).\n- **Side-effects (in order):** normalize address/email/telephone; resolve+roll-forward registration date; assign customerCode, membershipNumber, householdId, householdMemberCount, namesakeCount, bulkSignupWarning, possibleDuplicate; persist owner; record idempotency key; write audit log; return 201 with Location header.\n\nNote the two escalations `MethodArgumentNotValidException` and `DataIntegrityViolationException` also have handlers, so schema-bind failures and DB constraint violations map to error responses rather than 500s. I didn't change anything."
